<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 11 and earlier backup rules.

  Two directories are excluded, for two different reasons.

  credentials/ holds the GitHub credential, encrypted under a key that lives in
  the Android Keystore and never leaves the device, so a restored copy on
  another device could not be decrypted anyway. Excluding it keeps that from
  being the user's problem to discover: they would see "Connected" against a
  credential that fails closed on first use. It also keeps the ciphertext out of
  Google's backup transport entirely, which is the stronger property.

  picoclaw/ is Core's private state directory: config.json and .security.yml.
  Android onboarding declines credential encryption, so .security.yml holds
  provider API keys and channel bot tokens as plaintext. Those are 0600 and
  app-private, which stops another app reading them — but says nothing about
  backup, and without this exclusion they were copied verbatim into Google's
  cloud backup and into device-to-device transfer.

  RECHECK AFTER THE PICOCLAW -> POCKETCLAW NAMESPACE MIGRATION. This path is
  matched by name. If PocketClawService.buildEnvironment's internalHome is ever
  renamed from "picoclaw", this line silently stops matching and every secret
  becomes backup-eligible again with no test failing on its own.
  backup_rules_test.dart is what makes that failure loud.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="credentials/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="picoclaw/" />
</full-backup-content>
